    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0564" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg490"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. McCook.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 24, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 4, of 1st of August last,
                    in relation to the visit of Queen Emma to the United States, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to state that your judicious suggestion in regard to bestowing on
                    her similar attentions to those which she received in England has been
                    anticipated by the President.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward M. McCook,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
